Hardening harness
=================

Two scripts on top of the unit tests, for the checks "make test" alone
doesn't do. Both work for a native build and for a cross build tested
on the build host through a sysroot.

run - runtime checkers
----------------------

    unit/hardening/run [-c compiler]... [asan|tsan|valgrind]...

Rebuilds the plugin, the extension library and the unit tests from
clean for each checker and runs "make test" with:

  asan       AddressSanitizer + UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, any report
             is fatal, leaks included
  tsan       ThreadSanitizer, with ASLR off as TSan needs
  valgrind   memcheck; fails on any error or definite leak (the
             "make -C unit valgrind" target only reports)

Pass -c once per compiler to build the sanitizer runs with (GCC and
Clang find different things). Logs go to unit/hardening/logs.

Cross build, run on the build host through the sysroot's loader:

    PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR=$SYSROOT \
    PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR=$SYSROOT/usr/lib/pkgconfig:$SYSROOT/usr/share/pkgconfig \
    TEST_RUNNER="$SYSROOT/usr/lib/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 --library-path $SYSROOT/usr/lib" \
    unit/hardening/run -c "x86_64-linux-gcc --sysroot=$SYSROOT" \
        -c "clang --target=x86_64-linux-gnu --sysroot=$SYSROOT"

The sysroot needs the sanitizer runtimes (libasan, libubsan, libtsan;
compiler-rt for Clang). TEST_RUNNER is also honoured by the plain
"make test", "make test-debug" and "make valgrind" targets in unit/.

static-analysis - analyzers and warnings on every target
--------------------------------------------------------

    unit/hardening/static-analysis [-c name=compiler]... [-u]

Runs gcc -fanalyzer (-O0 and -O2), clang --analyze with the alpha
checkers, clang-tidy, cppcheck (exhaustive), flawfinder and sparse over
src/ and lib/src/, and compiles everything with each -c compiler using
-Wall -Wextra -Wshadow -Wformat=2 -Wcast-align -Wpointer-arith -Wvla.
Build with GCC and Clang for each supported target: armv7 is 32-bit
and catches what the 64-bit targets don't. A compiler command with
--sysroot= gets pkg-config pointed at that sysroot.

Findings are compared, without line numbers, with
static-analysis.baseline, where every accepted finding carries the
reason it was accepted. Anything new fails the run; baseline entries
that went away are listed so they can be dropped. -u regenerates the
baseline from the current run, keeping the reasons of the entries that
are still there and marking the new ones "TODO" - review those, fix
what's real and explain the rest before committing.

The baseline was produced with GCC 15, Clang 21, cppcheck 2.19,
flawfinder 2.0.19 and sparse 0.6.4 against Sailfish OS ofono headers;
other versions report somewhat different sets.

Adding tests
------------

New unit tests go in unit/unit_<name>/ like the existing ones, and in
unit/Makefile and unit/coverage/run. A test for a fix should fail with
the fix reverted; check that before relying on it.
